@startuml f2-automation-submits-task
title F2 — Automation submits a task (REST -> Event Router)

|Auto|
start
:POST /auth/login to API Gateway;
note right
  Automation authenticates with GW
  to get a bearer token.
  This is the only time Auto talks to GW.
end note

|API Gateway|
:Validate credentials;
:Issue bearer_token;

|Auto|
:Receive bearer_token;
:Build task payload
 (prompt, tools[], secret_ids[]);
:REST POST /tasks
 (bearer_token, payload)
 to Event Router;

|ER|
:Validate bearer_token;
:Validate schema;
:Validate secret_ids belong to caller's project;

|SS|
:open env (validate secret_ids exist for project);
note right
  Existence + authz check only.
  No values returned here.
end note

|SS|
:Return ok;

|ER|
:Build scope = HMAC(project_id, task_id, secret_ids, TTL);
:Persist task
 (status=queued,
  scope_token,
  routing_target,
  payload,
  project_id)
 in ER DB;
:Return 202 { task_id };

|Auto|
:Receive 202;
:Store task_id for later correlation;

stop

note right
  Auto authenticates with GW (one call),
  then bypasses GW for data plane.
  ER is the single entry point for task creation.
  ER DB is the only state target on submit.
  No queues - the pending task is just
  a row in the ER DB.
end note

@enduml